From 8bcec904fcaf87974ec1ca1e81f8c51c1f34bcb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:16:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 41/43] Multithreaded engine: start the thread search at every
 non-efficiency core

With numThreads=0 the engine timed 0.15 s windows starting at the core
count of hw.perflevel0 and went up by two. On a chip whose second core
class is nearly as fast as the first (M5 Pro: 5 "Super" + 10
"Performance" cores) the search needed eight windows to reach 15
threads, and short runs lost 4 to 19 % to it.

The search now starts at the number of cores whose hw.perflevelN.name
is not "Efficiency" (15 on that chip, still 4 on a 4 + 6 M5) and steps
down by two while every step is the fastest so far, then tries the
neighbours of the best. Three windows instead of eight on the 5.25 M
notch model. OPENEMS_TUNE_START=p keeps the old rule.

Scheduling only: probes are identical to v0.37.0 on six models at
fixed and automatic thread counts.

Generated-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
Signed-off-by: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
